{"icbeb2018_dataset": "The ICBEB2018 dataset is a collection of electrocardiogram (ECG) data used for benchmarking and evaluating algorithmic solutions in the field of arrhythmia detection and other ECG-related tasks.|Here is another description: The ICBEB2018 dataset is a large collection of 12-lead electrocardiograms (ECGs) used for research in ECG classification. It contains 6877 ECG records, each annotated by up to three reviewers with up to three statements from a set of nine classes.|Here is another description: The ICBEB2018 dataset is a large collection of electrocardiogram (ECG) data that was released for the 1st China Physiological Signal Challenge 2018, held during the 7th International Conference on Biomedical Engineering and Biotechnology. It serves as a valuable resource for research in ECG classification and analysis.|Here is another description: The ICBEB2018 dataset is a collection of electrocardiogram (ECG) data used for research and analysis in the field of cardiology. It includes various types of ECG recordings that are categorized based on different cardiac conditions."},
