{"ecg_statements": "ECG statements are annotations, diagnostic labels, or interpretations derived from electrocardiogram (ECG) data. They describe various aspects of the heart's electrical activity and are crucial for diagnosing cardiac conditions. These statements can be standardized according to specific protocols like the SCP-ECG standard and are essential for interpreting ECG records and identifying abnormalities such as bundle branch blocks, atrial fibrillation, and ST segment changes.|Here is another description: ECG statements refer to specific observations or interpretations derived from an electrocardiogram, a test that records the electrical activity of the heart. These statements can vary in specificity and are used to diagnose or monitor cardiac conditions."},
