{"non_specific_st_depression": "Non-specific ST depression refers to a pattern observed on an ECG where the ST segment, which is the flat, isoelectric section of the ECG between the S wave and T wave, is depressed below the baseline. This can indicate various underlying cardiac conditions but is termed \"non-specific\" because it does not point to a single, definitive diagnosis."},
