{"enlarging_kernel_sizes_to_5": "Enlarging kernel sizes to 5 refers to a modification in the architecture of neural networks, specifically increasing the size of the convolutional filters from a smaller size to 5. This change is implemented to potentially enhance the network's ability to capture more detailed features from the input data."},
{"enlarging_kernel_sizes_to_5__improved__the_performance": "The predicate \"improved\" indicates that the action of enlarging kernel sizes to 5 had a positive effect on a certain aspect of the system or process. In this context, it suggests that the modification led to better outcomes or results."},
