{"evaluating_on_the_whole_test_set": "Evaluating on the whole test set means assessing the performance of classifiers using all available data in the test set. This process provides a comprehensive measure of how well the classifiers perform on unseen data, which is critical for understanding their generalizability and effectiveness."},
{"lower_and_upper_confidence_intervals": "The lower and upper confidence intervals are statistical measures used to express the range within which the true value of a parameter is expected to lie with a certain level of confidence. In the context of evaluating classifier performance, these intervals help in assessing the uncertainty and variability of the performance metrics."},
