{"bootstrap_estimates_of_the_difference": "Bootstrap estimates of the difference refer to statistical measures calculated through the bootstrap method, which involves resampling with replacement from the original dataset to estimate the distribution of a statistic. In this context, these estimates are used to assess the performance differences between classifiers."},
{"bootstrap_estimates_of_the_difference__are_calculated_for__the_best_performing_and_all_other_classifiers": "The phrase \"are calculated for\" indicates the purpose or application of the bootstrap estimates. Here, it specifies that the bootstrap estimates are being computed to evaluate and compare the performance metrics of different classifiers."},
{"the_best_performing_and_all_other_classifiers": "The best-performing and all other classifiers refer to a set of machine learning models that have been trained and evaluated on a given dataset. The best-performing classifier is the one that achieved the highest score according to the chosen performance metrics, while all other classifiers are the remaining models that were compared against the best one."},
{"confidence_intervals_for_the_difference": "The confidence intervals for the difference refer to the statistical measure used to assess the uncertainty of the difference between the best-performing classifier and other classifiers in the evaluation. These intervals are derived through empirical bootstrapping on the test set."},
{"confidence_intervals_for_the_difference__do_not_cover__zero": "The predicate \"do not cover\" indicates that the confidence intervals calculated for the difference between classifiers do not include the value zero. This suggests a statistically significant difference between the classifiers at a confidence level of 0.05."},
