{"only_the_point_estimate_and_the_maximal_absolute_deviation_between_point_estimate_and_lower_and_upper_bound": "Only the point estimate and the maximal absolute deviation between point estimate and lower and upper bound refers to the specific data points usually included in summary tables. The point estimate represents the central value of a metric, while the maximal absolute deviation provides a measure of the uncertainty or variability around this estimate, helping to convey the reliability of the reported results."},
