{"bootstrap_process": "The bootstrap process is a statistical method used to estimate the uncertainty of a classifier's performance by repeatedly sampling with replacement from the original dataset. In this context, it is employed to generate 95% confidence intervals for performance metrics on the test set."},
{"bootstrap_process__does_not_guarantee__that_at_least_one_positive_sample_for_each_class_is_contained_in_each_bootstrap_sample": "The bootstrap process does not guarantee that each bootstrap sample will contain at least one positive sample for each class. This is due to the random nature of the sampling with replacement, which can lead to some classes being underrepresented or entirely absent in certain bootstrap samples."},
