{"metrics_such_as_the_term_centric_macro_auc": "Metrics such as the term-centric macro-AUC are performance evaluation metrics used to assess the effectiveness of classification algorithms, particularly in scenarios where multiple classes are involved and balanced performance across classes is desired."},
{"metrics_such_as_the_term_centric_macro_auc__cannot_be_evaluated_if__at_least_one_positive_sample_for_each_class_is_not_contained_in_each_bootstrap_sample": "The predicate \"cannot be evaluated if\" indicates a condition under which the subject metrics are inapplicable or invalid. This suggests that certain prerequisites must be met for these metrics to provide meaningful insights into the performance of a classification model."},
{"at_least_one_positive_sample_for_each_class_is_not_contained_in_each_bootstrap_sample": "At least one positive sample for each class being not contained in each bootstrap sample refers to a scenario in bootstrapping where, due to random sampling, some classes may not be represented in a given bootstrap sample. This absence of representation can lead to the inability to calculate certain performance metrics accurately."},
{"bootstrap_samples_without_at_least_one_positive_sample_for_each_class": "Bootstrap samples that do not contain at least one positive sample for each class are problematic in the context of evaluating certain metrics, such as the term-centric macro-AUC, as these metrics require representation from all classes to be accurately assessed."},
{"bootstrap_samples_without_at_least_one_positive_sample_for_each_class__are__discarded_and_redrawn_until_the_condition_is_met": "The process described involves ensuring that each bootstrap sample meets a specific condition\u2014namely, containing at least one positive sample for each class. This is crucial for the valid evaluation of certain performance metrics."},
