{"ptb_xl_dataset__underlies__most_experiments_presented_below": "The term \"underlies\" indicates that the PTB-XL dataset forms the basis or fundamental support for the majority of the experiments discussed in the context. It suggests that the dataset is a critical component in the design, execution, and analysis of these experiments."},
{"most_experiments_presented_below": "The phrase \"most experiments presented below\" refers to a series of research studies or trials that are detailed further in the document. These experiments rely heavily on the PTB-XL dataset for their data and analysis, making the dataset an essential element in their methodology and results."},
{"ptb_xl_dataset__contains__diagnostic_superclasses": "The predicate \"contains\" signifies that the PTB-XL dataset includes or comprises various categories or groups within its structure. This relationship indicates that the dataset is organized into distinct sections or classes for easier analysis and understanding."},
{"diagnostic_superclasses": "Diagnostic superclasses in the PTB-XL dataset refer to broad categories under which specific ECG diagnoses are grouped. These superclasses include normal ECG (_NORM_), myocardial infarction (_MI_), conduction disturbance (_CD_), ST/T-changes (_STTC_), and hypertrophy (_HYP_), each representing a significant diagnostic area in cardiology."},
{"norm": "_NORM is a diagnostic superclass within the PTB-XL dataset, representing a category of electrocardiogram (ECG) readings.|Here is another description: NORM is an abbreviation used in the context of the ICBEB2018 dataset to denote a specific type of electrocardiogram (ECG) result."},
{"norm__stands_for__normal_ecg": "The predicate \"stands for\" indicates that _NORM is an abbreviation or shorthand notation used to represent a specific condition or category within the dataset.|Here is another description: The predicate \"stands for\" indicates that NORM is an acronym or shorthand notation representing a more detailed term or concept, in this case, related to ECG results."},
{"normal_ecg": "Normal ECG refers to an electrocardiogram that shows no significant abnormalities, indicating a healthy heart rhythm and electrical activity.|Here is another description: Normal ECG refers to an electrocardiogram that shows no abnormalities or deviations from the standard patterns expected in a healthy individual's heart rhythm and electrical activity."},
{"mi": "_MI is an abbreviation used in the context of the PTB-XL dataset to represent a specific diagnostic superclass related to heart conditions."},
{"mi__stands_for__myocardial_infarction": "The phrase'stands for' indicates that _MI is an acronym or shorthand notation that represents the full term'myocardial infarction' within the dataset's classification system."},
{"myocardial_infarction": "Myocardial infarction, commonly known as a heart attack, is a serious medical condition where there is a lack of blood flow to the heart muscle, leading to damage or death of parts of the heart muscle due to oxygen deprivation."},
{"cd": "_CD refers to a category within the PTB-XL dataset that is used to classify electrocardiograms (ECGs) based on specific diagnostic criteria. It is one of several superclasses used in the dataset to summarize ECG diagnoses."},
{"cd__stands_for__conduction_disturbance": "The phrase \"stands for\" indicates that _CD is an abbreviation or shorthand notation representing a more detailed term or concept, in this case, conduction disturbance."},
{"conduction_disturbance": "Conduction disturbance refers to abnormalities in the electrical conduction system of the heart, which can be detected through an electrocardiogram (ECG). These disturbances can affect the heart's rhythm and are an important diagnostic category in cardiology."},
{"sttc": "_STTC is a diagnostic superclass within the PTB-XL dataset, representing a category of electrocardiogram (ECG) findings."},
{"sttc__stands_for__st_t_changes": "The predicate 'stands for' indicates that _STTC is an abbreviation or shorthand notation for a specific term or concept, in this case, ST/T-changes."},
{"st_t_changes": "ST/T-changes refer to alterations in the ST segment and T wave of an electrocardiogram, which can indicate various cardiac conditions or responses to physiological or pathological stimuli."},
{"hyp": "_HYP is an abbreviation used in the context of the PTB-XL dataset to represent a specific diagnostic superclass related to electrocardiograms (ECGs)."},
