{"hypertrophy": "Hypertrophy refers to the thickening of the heart muscle, which can be detected through ECG readings. It is one of the diagnostic superclasses in the PTB-XL dataset, indicating a condition where the heart muscle has enlarged."},
{"dataset": "The dataset is a large collection of clinical electrocardiogram (ECG) records, specifically designed for the training and evaluation of machine learning algorithms. It is notable for its size, being the largest publicly accessible clinical ECG dataset to date, and for its rich set of annotations and metadata.|Here is another description: The dataset in question is a collection of 6877 12-lead ECGs, each lasting between 6 and 60 seconds, annotated by up to three reviewers from a set of nine classes.|Here is another description: The dataset refers to a collection of data that has been compiled and organized for analysis or reference. In this context, it is a specific set of data that has been prepared for publication.|Here is another description: The dataset is a collection of data that has been published in a scientific journal. It is a resource for researchers to use in their studies.|Here is another description: The dataset refers to a collection of data that has been compiled and organized for analysis or reference. In this context, it is specifically mentioned in a scientific publication.|Here is another description: The dataset refers to a collection of scientific data published in a specific journal.|Here is another description: The dataset is a collection of scientific data published in a peer-reviewed journal."},
