{"diag__related_to__diagnostic_statements": "The predicate \"related to\" signifies the association between the category _diag_ and the diagnostic statements. It indicates that the _diag_ category encompasses or is connected to various diagnostic interpretations derived from the ECG records."},
{"diagnostic_statements": "The object \"diagnostic statements\" refers to the specific annotations within the ECG dataset that describe various cardiac conditions or abnormalities detected in the ECG records. These statements are part of the SCP-ECG standard and are used to provide detailed diagnostic information.|Here is another description: Diagnostic statements refer to specific annotations within the ECG records that indicate particular medical conditions or findings, such as \"anterior myocardial infarction.\" These statements are part of a larger set of annotations used to describe various aspects of the ECG, including rhythm and form changes.|Here is another description: Diagnostic statements refer to specific medical interpretations derived from ECG records, such as identifying conditions like \"anterior myocardial infarction.\" These statements are crucial for clinical diagnosis and are part of a larger dataset that includes various types of ECG annotations.|Here is another description: Diagnostic statements refer to specific medical or clinical observations and conclusions made by healthcare professionals about a patient's condition. These statements are crucial for accurate diagnosis and treatment planning.|Here is another description: Diagnostic statements are textual data that describe medical diagnoses. These statements serve as the training dataset for the model, allowing it to learn patterns, relationships, and uncertainties associated with medical diagnoses."},
{"form": "The subject '_form_' refers to a category within the ECG annotation system that focuses on the morphology or shape of specific segments in an electrocardiogram. It is one of the three non-mutually exclusive categories used for annotating ECG records in the dataset."},
{"form__related_to__notable_changes_of_particular_segments_within_the_ecg": "The predicate 'related to' indicates an association or connection between the subject '_form_' and the object, which in this case are the notable changes observed in particular segments of an ECG. It signifies that the '_form_' category is concerned with these specific changes."},
{"notable_changes_of_particular_segments_within_the_ecg": "The object 'notable changes of particular segments within the ECG' describes the specific focus of the '_form_' category. These changes could include abnormalities in the QRS complex, T-waves, or other segments of the ECG that are critical for diagnosing certain cardiac conditions."},
