{"each_ecg_record__annotated_by__up_to_three_statements_by_up_to_three_reviewers": "Annotated by indicates the process through which each ECG record is evaluated and labeled by reviewers. This process involves the assignment of diagnostic statements to each record based on the reviewers' assessments."},
{"up_to_three_statements_by_up_to_three_reviewers": "Up to three statements by up to three reviewers refers to the detailed evaluation process where each ECG record can receive up to three diagnostic statements, each provided by one of up to three different reviewers. These statements are selected from a predefined set of nine classes, which include one normal and eight abnormal classes."},
