{"stratified_sampling": "Stratified sampling is a method of sampling that involves dividing a population into smaller groups, or strata, and then selecting a sample from each stratum in proportion to its size relative to the population. This technique ensures that each subgroup of the population is adequately represented in the sample."},
{"stratified_sampling__preserving__the_overall_label_distribution_in_each_fold": "Preserving in the context of stratified sampling refers to the process of maintaining the proportional representation of different categories or labels within each sample or fold. This ensures that the sample accurately reflects the diversity and distribution of the original population."},
