{"atrial_fibrillation": "Atrial fibrillation is a common heart condition characterized by an irregular and often rapid heart rate that can lead to poor blood flow. It is a significant focus in cardiology, especially in the interpretation of ECG results."},
{"1avb": "1AVB is an abbreviation used in the context of electrocardiogram (ECG) statements to denote a specific type of heart condition."},
