{"precomputed_statistical_features": "Precomputed statistical features are derived metrics from raw data, such as Fourier or Wavelet coefficients, which capture essential characteristics of the data. These features are used as inputs for the classifier to make predictions, enhancing the model's ability to generalize from the training data to new, unseen data.|Here is another description: Precomputed statistical features refer to data that has been previously calculated and stored for use in various analyses, such as in machine learning models or signal processing tasks."},
{"precomputed_statistical_features__include__fourier_or_wavelet_coefficients": "The term 'include' in this context signifies that the set of precomputed statistical features encompasses or contains certain elements, specifically mentioning Fourier or Wavelet coefficients as part of this set."},
{"fourier_or_wavelet_coefficients": "Fourier or Wavelet coefficients are numerical values derived from the application of Fourier or Wavelet transforms to a signal. These coefficients represent the signal in the frequency domain and are often used in signal processing and analysis to extract meaningful features."},
