{"preprocessing__include__removing_baseline_wander_and_or_filtering": "The predicate 'include' signifies that certain actions or steps are part of a broader process or methodology. In this context, it indicates that specific preprocessing techniques are considered within the scope of data preparation methods."},
{"removing_baseline_wander_and_or_filtering": "Removing baseline wander and/or filtering are common preprocessing techniques used in signal processing to improve the quality of time series data. Baseline wander removal corrects slow variations in the signal baseline, while filtering helps to eliminate noise and unwanted frequency components, thereby enhancing the signal for analysis.|Here is another description: Removing baseline wander and/or filtering refers to preprocessing techniques applied to time series data to eliminate noise and improve signal quality. These methods are often utilized to enhance the performance of analytical models by cleaning the data before analysis.|Here is another description: Removing baseline wander and/or filtering refers to preprocessing techniques applied to time series data to eliminate noise and improve signal quality. These methods are often utilized in various literature approaches to enhance the performance of classifiers or models."},
