{"summary_tables__typically_report__only_the_point_estimate_and_the_maximal_absolute_deviation_between_point_estimate_and_lower_and_upper_bound": "Typically report signifies the common practice or standard method used in summary tables to present specific types of data. In this context, it refers to the usual way of reporting point estimates and their associated deviations in performance metrics."},
{"only_the_point_estimate_and_the_maximal_absolute_deviation_between_point_estimate_and_lower_and_upper_bound": "The point estimate and the maximal absolute deviation between the point estimate and lower and upper bound represent the central value of a performance metric and the maximum difference between this central value and the confidence interval bounds. This format allows for a compact representation of both the metric's value and its uncertainty, providing a clear understanding of the performance and its variability."},
