{"0_743_09__is_understood_as__0_743_0_009": "The predicate \"is understood as\" indicates the interpretation or meaning of the subject value. In this context, it explains how the point estimate should be read and understood in terms of its associated confidence interval."},
{"0_743_0_009": "The object \"0.743 \u00b1 0.009\" represents the point estimate value along with its 95% confidence interval, derived through empirical bootstrapping with 10,000 iterations on the test set. This provides a measure of the uncertainty associated with the point estimate."},
{"sparsely_populated_classes": "Sparsely populated classes refer to categories or groups within a dataset that contain a relatively small number of instances or samples. In the context of machine learning and evaluation metrics, these classes can pose challenges due to their limited representation."},
{"sparsely_populated_classes__are_not_excluded_from__the_evaluation": "The phrase \"are not excluded from\" indicates that despite potential challenges or limitations, certain entities or elements are still considered or included in a process or evaluation. In this context, it means that even though sparsely populated classes may present difficulties, they are still part of the evaluation process."},
{"the_evaluation": "The evaluation in this context refers to the process of assessing the performance and effectiveness of machine learning models or classifiers. It involves using various metrics and procedures to determine how well the models can generalize and make accurate predictions on new, unseen data."},
{"stratified_sampling_procedure": "The stratified sampling procedure is a method used to ensure that each subset of a given population will be proportionally represented in the sample. This technique is particularly useful in maintaining the integrity of statistical analysis by preserving the distribution of key variables across different groups."},
