{"auc_curves_for_two_subset_of_samples": "AUC curves for two subsets of samples refer to the graphical representation of the Area Under the Curve (AUC) values calculated for two different groups or categories within a dataset. These curves are commonly used in machine learning and statistics to evaluate the performance of a classification model by plotting the true positive rate against the false positive rate at various threshold settings."},
