{"deaths_in_middle_aged_adults": "Deaths in middle-aged adults refer to the mortality rates among individuals aged between 45 and 64 years. This demographic is often studied to understand the impact of various health factors and lifestyle choices on mortality."},
{"deaths_in_middle_aged_adults__studied_in__21_countries_from_five_continents": "The predicate \"studied in\" indicates that the subject, deaths in middle-aged adults, was the focus of a research study conducted across multiple locations. This research aimed to gather data and analyze the factors contributing to mortality in this age group."},
{"21_countries_from_five_continents": "The object \"21 countries from five continents\" specifies the geographical scope of the study. This extensive coverage across multiple continents allowed for a comprehensive analysis of how regional differences, cultural practices, and environmental factors influence mortality rates in middle-aged adults."},
