{"2019": "The year 2019 was marked by significant publications and events across various fields, including the release of the National Ambulatory Medical Care Survey: 2016 National Summary Tables, advancements in arrhythmia detection using deep neural networks, time series classification, and neural engineering. Notable events included the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, the Proc. Int. Conf. Learn. Representations where the \"ADAM\" paper was presented, the 32nd edition of Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, a research study on infarction detection using fully convolutional neural networks, and the Mach. Learn. Health (ML4H) at NeurIPS workshop.|Here is another description: 2019 is the year when the book \"Explainable AI: Interpreting, Explaining and Visualizing Deep Learning\" was published by Springer International Publishing."},
