{"qt_rr_curvatures": "QT/RR curvatures refer to the relationship between the QT interval and the RR interval in electrocardiograms, which are important for understanding cardiac repolarization. These curvatures are analyzed to assess cardiac function and potential arrhythmic risks.|Here is another description: QT/RR curvatures are measurements related to the electrical activity of the heart, specifically the QT interval adjusted for heart rate (RR interval). These curvatures are important in assessing cardiac function and can vary among individuals.|Here is another description: QT/RR curvatures are measurements related to the electrical activity of the heart, specifically concerning the QT interval and its relationship with the RR interval. These curvatures are important in assessing cardiac function and can vary based on different factors, including sex and various covariates."},
