{"hierarchical_decomposition_of_class_specific_aucs": "The hierarchical decomposition of class-specific AUCs refers to a method of breaking down the performance metrics (AUCs) of different classes into a hierarchical structure. This involves analyzing the performance at various levels of classification, from broad categories down to specific subclasses and individual diagnostic statements, to reveal hidden stratifications in algorithmic performance."},
{"hierarchical_decomposition": "Hierarchical decomposition is a method used to break down complex data into more manageable and analyzable parts. In the context of performance metrics, it allows for a detailed examination of how different subcomponents contribute to the overall result."},
