{"auc_curves_for_two_subset_of_samples": "AUC curves for two subsets of samples are graphical representations used to evaluate the performance of a binary classifier system as its discrimination threshold is varied. In this context, the AUC (Area Under the Curve) curves are being used to reveal hidden stratification within a specific class, indicating how well the classifier can distinguish between different groups of samples."},
