{"weak_performance": "Weak performance in this context refers to the classifier's inability to accurately categorize certain ECG statements, particularly those that are non-specific or heterogeneous in nature. This performance deficiency is noted when examining specific subclasses within the ECG hierarchy, rather than just the overall or superclass performance.|Here is another description: The weak performance refers to the inadequate results of a discriminative classifier on specific ECG statements, such as _NST__, _LAO/LAE_, and _IVCD_, which are located in the bottom layer of the hierarchy."},
