{"only_the_corresponding_superclass_or_subclass_performance_measures": "The corresponding superclass or subclass performance measures are the reported metrics that evaluate the performance of the classifier on broader or more specific categories, which do not reveal the weak performance on individual ECG statements."},
{"findings_for_nst_and_ivcd": "The subject refers to the findings related to non-specific ST changes (NST) and non-specific intraventricular conduction disturbance (IVCD) in electrocardiogram (ECG) readings. These findings are part of a broader analysis of ECG statement classifications and their impact on classifier performance."},
{"findings_for_nst_and_ivcd__can_be_explained_by__both_statements_are_by_definition_non_specific_ecg_statements_and_potentially_subsume_rather_heterogeneous_groups_of_findings": "The predicate indicates that the observed findings for NST and IVCD can be explained by certain characteristics inherent to these ECG statements. It suggests a causal or explanatory relationship between the nature of these ECG statements and the observed findings."},
{"both_statements_are_by_definition_non_specific_ecg_statements_and_potentially_subsume_rather_heterogeneous_groups_of_findings": "The object describes the nature of the ECG statements NST and IVCD. It states that both are by definition non-specific and potentially encompass a diverse range of findings. This non-specificity and heterogeneity are proposed as reasons for the observed findings in the classifier's performance."},
{"hidden_stratification__is_straightforward_to_identify__in_hindsight": "The phrase \"is straightforward to identify\" indicates that, once the outcomes are known, recognizing hidden stratification within diagnostic labels is relatively easy and clear-cut. This suggests that the complexity lies more in the initial detection rather than in understanding it post facto."},
{"in_hindsight": "In hindsight signifies the ease of identifying hidden stratification after the fact, when the results and classifications are already known. It implies that the recognition of such stratification becomes simpler when one can look back on the data and outcomes with the benefit of prior knowledge."},
{"hidden_stratification__is_demonstrated_by__55": "The phrase \"is demonstrated by\" indicates that the concept of hidden stratification is exemplified or shown through a specific method or example. In this context, it refers to the use of an unsupervised clustering approach to reveal the presence of hidden stratification in sample groups."},
