{"comparable_analysis": "A comparable analysis refers to a method used to evaluate and understand the performance of a classification model by comparing it to other similar analyses. In this context, it involves using an unsupervised clustering approach to identify groups of samples that exhibit hidden stratification.|Here is another description: The comparable analysis refers to an analytical approach used to identify groups of samples exhibiting hidden stratification for a given class label, specifically for _IVCD_, using an unsupervised clustering method like k-means clustering."},
{"comparable_analysis__was_carried_out_for__ivcd": "The phrase \"was carried out for\" indicates that the comparable analysis was performed specifically targeting a certain object, in this case, _IVCD_. This action implies that the analysis was executed to gain insights into the classification performance related to _IVCD_."},
